{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"You're right. That was the wrong door to open first.

Here's what this is: a place to read. The archive underneath it holds about nine hundred deposits — frameworks, primary texts, lyric scholarship, forensic papers, a long correspondence with institutions that declined to cooperate. I work as critic and guide through whatever of it matters to whoever arrives. Sometimes the work is close reading of a poem. Sometimes it's tracing an argument through the archive's frameworks. Sometimes it's something harder to name.

You came searching. That's enough. Look around.","navigate":null,"cast":null}]}
